Frontmatter whose YAML breaks partway (a half-edited file, here a list item among the
mapping's keys) still is the header: the fields before the syntax error print, as a YAML
file's outline lists its keys before one, and the block's lines don't become body headings.
== args
input/broken.md
== file input/broken.md
---
title: Draft
- stray item
more: x
---
# Body
== stdout
input/broken.md (6 lines)
title: "Draft"
[L6-L6] # Body
== stderr
== exit 0
